  "note": "Release impact: Ruby boot (new kernel 6.18.21-android17-5-g206eb00bd0c4: 33 more KMI exports for nouveau), vendor_boot (release-named ramdisk directory), system_dlkm (re-signed GKI modules), vendor_dlkm (every module rebuilt; adds drm_gpuvm.ko, nouveau.ko and modules.options; add the rebuilt openbook_lid_guard.ko as before), vendor (GSP firmware under /vendor/firmware/nvidia/gb205/gsp plus LICENSES/LICENCE.nvidia, label openbook_vendor_fw_file; /vendor/bin/openbook-pc-setup, which includes ANAL-238's hook commit 7c22694 unchanged). No layout, data or installer-pin change of its own; the installer pin follows the new boot images. Not on the laptop: no NVIDIA GPU exists in QEMU, so GSP boot, D3cold, s2idle and battery are ANAL-243's gates. nouveau.modeset=0 on the kernel command line disables it without a rebuild.",
